beats.content:
`theme.json` is optional, but almost every block theme has one. It has two main sections:

- `settings` decides which controls and presets (such as a colour palette) the editor offers.
- `styles` applies the theme's design, using those presets.

Here is a small but complete `theme.json` with a three-colour palette:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://schemas.wp.org/trunk/theme.json",
  "version": 3,
  "settings": {
    "color": {
      "palette": [
        { "name": "Base", "slug": "base", "color": "#ffffff" },
        { "name": "Contrast", "slug": "contrast", "color": "#1e1e1e" },
        { "name": "Subtle", "slug": "subtle", "color": "#f0f0f0" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

- `version` is the schema version. **3** is current: it arrived in WordPress 6.6 and is still current in WordPress 7.1. (Some handbook pages still show `2`, an older version WordPress still accepts.)
- `$schema` is optional. It lets your code editor check the file and suggest keys as you type.
- Each palette entry takes exactly three keys: `name` (the label people see), `slug` (its ID) and `color` (the value). WordPress turns each entry into a CSS custom property, such as `--wp--preset--color--contrast`.

One catch: WordPress doesn't warn you about a mistyped key. An entry without a `color` key is quietly skipped, with no error at all.

referenceSolution.bugFix:
{
  "$schema": "https://schemas.wp.org/trunk/theme.json",
  "version": 3,
  "settings": {
    "useRootPaddingAwareAlignments": true,
    "color": {
      "palette": [
        { "name": "Base", "slug": "base", "color": "#ffffff" },
        { "name": "Contrast", "slug": "contrast", "color": "#1e1e1e" },
        { "name": "Subtle", "slug": "subtle", "color": "#f0f0f0" },
        { "name": "Accent", "slug": "accent", "color": "#3858e9" }
      ]
    },
    "layout": {
      "contentSize": "40rem",
      "wideSize": "64rem"
    },
    "typography": {
      "fontFamilies": [
        {
          "name": "System Sans",
          "slug": "system-sans",
          "fontFamily": "system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "styles": {
    "color": {
      "background": "var:preset|color|base",
      "text": "var:preset|color|contrast"
    },
    "spacing": {
      "padding": {
        "top": "0",
        "right": "1.5rem",
        "bottom": "0",
        "left": "1.5rem"
      }
    },
    "typography": {
      "fontFamily": "var:preset|font-family|system-sans",
      "lineHeight": "1.6"
    },
    "elements": {
      "link": {
        "color": { "text": "var:preset|color|accent" }
      },
      "heading": {
        "typography": { "fontWeight": "700", "lineHeight": "1.2" }
      }
    }
  },
  "templateParts": [
    { "name": "header", "title": "Header", "area": "header" },
    { "name": "footer", "title": "Footer", "area": "footer" }
  ]
}

